  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention: Public Health Preparedness and Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) Center for Preparedness and Response (CPR) staff work at CDC offices and in health departments to guide communities through public health crises. HHS/CDC/CPR also funds health departments to prepare and lead local responses to emergencies. Additionally, HHS/CDC/CPR fosters research and innovation in preparation for and response to public health emergencies.</narrative>
  </description>
